TITLE: The Factory

LOGLINE
When the last American pencil factory closes, three generations fight to save their legacy.

THE SUBJECTS
John Martinez - 68, worked here 45 years, union leader
Sarah Chen - 34, MBA trying to modernize operations  
Mike Thompson - 22, third generation worker facing unemployment

THE CONFLICT
Overseas competition destroyed the business model. Now workers want to buy the factory themselves.

EPISODE STRUCTURE
Episode 1: The Glory Days - archival footage from the 1980s
Episode 2: The Decline - automation eliminates jobs
Episode 3: The Fight - workers organize the buyout

ACCESS
Exclusive access to board meetings, union negotiations, and family dinners.

VISUAL STYLE
Industrial cinematography, handheld verite during tense moments.
